  "rule": "Every device is a 2-thick bar. Its far line has a doubled end, and positions are indexed from that end. Each border marker sits on the near side of exactly one device, aligned with index i, and so defines a mapping index i -> marker colour. Every device then shoots, for every mapped index, a ray of that colour. The ray leaves the near line at that index, runs perpendicular to the bar away from the far line, and continues to the grid border.",
  "scope": "Infer device-relative indices from isolated border markers and apply coloured outward rays to every oriented device.",
